<http://data.silknow.org/object/a589d6ff-cc23-3976-a12d-083ea9c803a1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Twelve-symbol dragon robe of silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>). Blue and yellow ground with a design of key patterns and bats in various shades of pink scattered over it; five-clawed dragons in gold thread, twelve symbols, a deep lower border of mountains and sea. Very long shaped sleeves with a wide flaring kesi cuff; the lower half is of yellow striped with dragons in roundel forms in damask weave. The robe is lined with pale blue silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a589d6ff-cc23-3976-a12d-083ea9c803a1> .

